+#### Keep on top — Stable
+
+A window can be **kept on top**: it stays above every window that is not, even while another window has focus or a new one opens. The user toggles it with the pin button in the title bar (`core/keep-on-top`); code calls `setAlwaysOnTop()` and reads `Window.alwaysOnTop`.
+
+```javascript
+wp.os.windowManager.setAlwaysOnTop( 'edit-php', true );
+wp.os.windowManager.getById( 'edit-php' ).alwaysOnTop; // true
+wp.os.windowManager.setAlwaysOnTop( 'edit-php', false ); // normal stacking again
+```
+
+- **Paint order, not focus.** Focusing a window underneath gives it focus (`getFocused()`, `os-window-focused`) but it still paints below the kept-on-top one.
+- **Several at once.** Windows kept on top stack among themselves in focus order, as ordinary windows do.
+- **Children come along.** A child of a kept-on-top window is lifted with it, so the owner still never sits above its child.
+- **Fullscreen still wins.** A fullscreen window covers everything, kept-on-top windows included.
+- **Persisted.** The flag is saved in the session (`alwaysOnTop: true`) and the window comes back kept on top after a reload. Unknown ids are a no-op, as is setting the value it already has.
+
